 # Changelog
 
-## 0.2.2 (2026-10-17)
+## 0.2.3 (2026-10-18)
+
+Additive API; one behaviour change (below). No existing signature, field or variant changed. Not compiled when written; verification is the CI run. The section below headed "0.2.2 (2026-10-17)" (several device ids, denylist, claims peek) is unpublished work on main and ships in this version; version 0.2.2 is already on the registry.
+
+- **`TokenSource` for `EngineEntitlements` (bogusyogi/rightkit#747).** New trait `TokenSource { fn read_token(&self) -> Result<Option<String>, String> }` (any matching closure works) and `EngineEntitlementsConfig::with_token_source`. `CredentialTokenSource::new(rightkit_credentials::Store, account)` (new optional feature `credential-token`, adds `rightkit-credentials`; default dependencies unchanged) reads the token from the OS credential store; a missing item is `NoLicense`, a store error is `Unreadable` with the store's message. There is deliberately no file-backed `TokenSource` (bogusyogi/rightkit#771 D4: no credentials in files); the existing default `license.token` read is unchanged. `Ok(None)` is `NoLicense`, `Err` is `Unreadable`; the text is trimmed, empty or over 16 KiB is refused, and the token is authenticated as before (signature, app, device, expiry). The source belongs to the engine process; it must not return a token pushed by a caller.
+- **Legacy v1 tokens (#747).** `verify_legacy_token(token, pubkey, app, &[device], now, sunset_unix)` accepts only `v == 1` and only while `now < sunset_unix` (the app's own cutoff); `verify_token_accepting_versions(.., accepted: &[u8])` accepts a chosen version set. Both return the new `#[non_exhaustive]` `VersionedVerifyError { UnsupportedVersion { got }, LegacySunset { sunset, now }, Verify(VerifyError) }`, and run the signature, app and device checks before the version and sunset checks. `LEGACY_TOKEN_VERSION` is `1`. `verify_token` is unchanged and still does not look at `v`.
+- **`plus` is `pro` (#747, #756 parity).** New `normalize_tier(&str) -> Option<&'static str>` (`plus` and `pro` give `pro`, `free` gives `free`, anything else `None`) and `Entitlement::normalized_tier()`. Behaviour change: `Entitlement::is_pro()` is now true for a `plus` token, and `tier_at_least` / `satisfies` rank `plus` as `pro` on both sides, so a `plus` entitlement satisfies a `pro` requirement and `LicenseRequirement::tier("plus")` needs Pro. Matching is exact (no case folding); unknown tiers still fail closed. This matches `normalizeTier` in `@rightkit/license`.
+- Tests: `src/versioned.rs` unit tests (v1 before and at sunset, v2 refused by the legacy path, version filter, empty list, pass-through of expiry, device, app and key failures, forged token reveals nothing), `tests/engine.rs` (source token, none, error, empty, oversize, still authenticated), `tests/policy_contract.rs` (plus as pro), `normalize_tier` unit test. The existing tier-order, engine, lifecycle and refresh tests that used `plus` as the "below Pro" tier now use `free`.
+- Triage, no change: #391 (peek half) is already `peek_unverified_claims`; the process-tree half is `rightkit-child-process`. #610, #501, #164 are shipped as noted below. #272 needs backend registration data. #420 (installation identity, clone detection) is a new owner and is not started here.
+
+## 0.2.2 (2026-10-17, content now under 0.2.3)
 
 Additive; no existing signature, field, variant or behaviour changed, no dependency change. Not compiled when written; verification is the CI run.
 
